-- The trigger (n4): a hit becomes a cast at the impact. Twin of n4-trigger.bqn.
-- A bolt that casts on impact: the hit is a join, the payload spawns at the point of death, and the carrier is consumed in the same barrier.
-- The collision pass is the theta-join comprehension marking both sides; plain bolts break on impact; the trigger card is a standing rule — spawn the payload at the carrier's own pos and consume the carrier, one barrier.
-- The payload's parent records the trigger bolt's gather-time row, and that row no longer exists after the barrier — the intensional/extensional boundary (spec Open Questions, Identity), pinned here as data.
--! registry ../registries/n4-trigger.reg
--! expect-n 5
--! expect keys = 2 3 4 5 6
--! expect sparkBolt = 1 0 0 0 0
--! expect firebolt = 0 0 0 0 1
--! expect hit = 0 1 1 0 0
--! expect health = 0 22 22 0 0
--! expect damage = 3 0 0 0 3
--! expect parent = -1 -1 -1 -1 0
--! expect pos = 20 30 40 6 61 5 0 0 40 5

[ b & e , +Hit | b <- SparkBolt, e <- Enemy, dist(b, e) < 8 ]
Enemy & Hit , Health -= 3
SparkBolt & Hit & !Trigger , ~
def payload = SparkBolt & Trigger & Hit => spawn Firebolt at pos ; ~
